    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **38 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field following the codebase's established pattern for derived read-only owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a computed getter `getContactPreference()` that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it into the DTO automatically by name (no controller change needed).\n\nBoth new tests pass (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and no existing tests regressed.",
